# Response headers for the Cloudflare Workers static-assets deployment.
#
# Copied verbatim from public/ into dist/ at build time, which is the directory
# wrangler.jsonc points `assets` at. Cloudflare reads it from there; it is never
# served as a file itself.
#
# Every directive below was checked against the BUILT output rather than against
# the source, per the house rule. The counts quoted are from `dist/` and are the
# reason each directive is shaped the way it is.
#
# What this file CANNOT do: redirect http:// to https://. That happens at the
# edge, before any header rule is consulted, and is a zone setting
# (SSL/TLS -> Edge Certificates -> Always Use HTTPS). Strict-Transport-Security
# is deliberately absent here for the same reason: Cloudflare's HSTS control
# emits it, and setting it in two places is how the two drift apart.

/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; script-src https://static.cloudflareinsights.com; connect-src https://cloudflareinsights.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; font-src 'self'; img-src 'self'; base-uri 'none'; form-action 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), camera=(), microphone=(), payment=(), usb=()
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy: same-origin

# Notes on the policy above, directive by directive:
#
#   default-src 'none'   The site's own build ships zero JavaScript: 0 <script>
#                        tags across every page, 0 .js/.mjs/.map files in dist,
#                        and check:built asserts it. So the default is the
#                        strictest value that exists, and anything not listed
#                        below is refused outright.
#
#   script-src           Exactly one host, and it is not ours. Cloudflare Web
#                        Analytics is enabled on the zone, and Cloudflare injects
#                        its beacon into the HTML at the edge, AFTER the build.
#                        Nothing in this repository puts it there, which is
#                        precisely why it went unnoticed for so long: it is
#                        injected only for browser-like requests, so fetching the
#                        page with curl shows a clean document.
#
#                        Naming the host here is the point. A bare 'self' would
#                        not have allowed it, and the first version of this file
#                        did not name it at all, which blocked the analytics the
#                        site owner actually wants. Listing it means the exception
#                        is visible, deliberate, and the ONLY script origin that
#                        will ever run. Anything else - an injected script from a
#                        compromised feed included - is still inert.
#
#                        The beacon carries its own integrity hash, so the file
#                        is verified by the browser before it runs.
#
#   connect-src          Where the beacon sends its measurements. Without it the
#                        script loads and then silently fails to report, which
#                        looks like working analytics that collect nothing.
#
#   style-src            'unsafe-inline' is required today and is not cosmetic:
#                        dist carries 1283 inline style= attributes (every SVG
#                        map shape carries its own fill) and 29 inline <style>
#                        blocks (Astro's scoped styles, plus the per-period
#                        rules TimeMap generates). Removing it would unstyle the
#                        maps entirely. Astro 5.18 ships experimental.csp, which
#                        would hash these and let 'unsafe-inline' go; that is a
#                        separate change, not a security fix, and it is not made
#                        here.
#
#   font-src 'self'      11 woff2 files, all served from /_astro/. No font
#                        network is contacted, and this keeps it that way.
#
#   img-src 'self'       There are 0 <img> tags. This covers the favicon links
#                        only (96 of them, /favicon.svg and /favicon.ico), and
#                        blocks an injected tracking pixel.
#
#   base-uri 'none'      The site uses no <base>. An injected one would silently
#                        repoint all 1102 internal links.
#
#   form-action 'none'   There are no forms anywhere. Nothing should be able to
#                        post from this origin.
#
#   frame-ancestors      The site has no sensitive action to trick anyone into,
#                        but it also has no reason to be framed, and being
#                        framed inside a page that misattributes the data is a
#                        real way to damage a citation index. X-Frame-Options is
#                        deliberately not also sent: frame-ancestors supersedes
#                        it in every browser that matters.
#
#   nosniff              Stops a browser deciding that .txt or .xml is really
#                        something executable.
#
#   Referrer-Policy      The site links out 1013 times. Without this, the full
#                        path of a jurisdiction or news-category page is handed
#                        to every government publisher we cite. Origin-only is
#                        enough for them and tells them less about the reader.
#                        Not no-referrer, because some government hosts behave
#                        oddly when it is absent entirely.
#
#   Permissions-Policy   Denies features nothing here uses. interest-cohort is
#                        not listed: it was never standardised and now only
#                        produces console noise.

# Content-hashed build assets. The hash IS the version, so a changed file gets a
# changed URL and these can be cached for a year. Applied only to /_astro/*, and
# deliberately NOT to HTML, robots.txt or the sitemaps, which keep the
# revalidate-every-time default so a data refresh is visible immediately.
/_astro/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
